  "title": "Inside RBI's Proposed Model Risk Management Framework",
  "summary": "For most lenders, model risk management till now has meant credit scoring. A bureau-based scorecard, some NPA prediction analytics, periodic risk team review. The regulatory anchor was a single chapter in RBI's 2002 Credit Risk Management guidance. That chapter predates machine learning in Indian lending.The draft \"Guidance on Regulatory Principles for Model Risk Management, 2026,\" released on June 24, changes this baseline. It is open for public comment until July 24. The proposed framework cov",
